        ":question/id": "214450de-6c4e-5468-90b3-b289da0c12f3",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1348",
        ":question/problem": "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ n\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $p⊥q$, find the value of $n.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $p⊥q$ ($p$ and $q$ are perpendicular) if and only if $p\\cdot q=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 4+n\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =28-4n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 28-4n & =0 \\\\ 28 & =4n \\\\ n & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
